WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:05.170
Every MyWell user can read every station's
data, not just their own.

00:05.290 --> 00:09.898
This tutorial is about how to get at it: pick
an area on the map,

00:10.018 --> 00:13.018
then look at its trend and its statistics.

00:13.850 --> 00:16.538
Now we're on: Data trend.

00:16.658 --> 00:21.146
This page charts how readings change over time
across a whole area.

00:21.266 --> 00:26.162
It opens empty on purpose — you begin by
choosing a Monitoring Area.

00:26.983 --> 00:28.999
Your monitoring areas.

00:29.119 --> 00:32.335
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

00:32.455 --> 00:37.975
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

00:38.095 --> 00:40.471
or the built-in Example area.

00:41.283 --> 00:43.611
One line, over time.

00:43.731 --> 00:50.259
Once an area is chosen, Data trend draws its
readings as a line, bar or area chart —

00:50.379 --> 00:53.067
the shape of the water through the seasons.

00:53.187 --> 00:56.019
Narrow it further with the filters above.

00:56.850 --> 00:58.410
Read the chart.

00:58.530 --> 01:02.394
Below the map, this panel charts the stations
in view.

01:02.514 --> 01:09.762
Pick a measurement type, time range and chart
style (Line, Bar or Area) to explore the data.

01:10.583 --> 01:13.559
Now we're on: Data statistics.

01:13.679 --> 01:20.327
The same data as Data trend, shown as numbers
instead of a line: a per-station table of averages,

01:20.447 --> 01:23.927
highs and lows, with the map shaded to match.

01:24.750 --> 01:26.766
Your monitoring areas.

01:26.886 --> 01:30.102
A monitoring area is a saved set of stations.

01:30.222 --> 01:35.742
Open My Monitoring Areas to switch between
“All stations” and any area you've saved,

01:35.862 --> 01:38.238
or the built-in Example area.

01:39.050 --> 01:41.138
The numbers, ranked.

01:41.258 --> 01:48.722
Data statistics answers 'which stations, and how
much?' — a sortable table of each station's average,

01:48.842 --> 01:52.898
highest and lowest values, with the map shaded
to match.

01:53.717 --> 01:55.277
Read the chart.

01:55.397 --> 01:59.261
Below the map, this panel charts the stations
in view.

01:59.381 --> 02:06.629
Pick a measurement type, time range and chart
style (Line, Bar or Area) to explore the data.

02:07.450 --> 02:09.394
That is the whole page.

02:09.514 --> 02:14.170
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

02:14.290 --> 02:16.954
Thanks for helping look after our water.
